  "category" : "Assessment and Accountability",
  "createdAt" : 1758562610,
  "description" : "This dataset contains the number and percent of students in ACCESS for ELLs reporting elements 1, 2, 3, and 5 of Title III ESSA requirements from the year 2022 onward.\n\nMassachusetts administers the ACCESS for ELLs test annually to all English learners in publicly funded K-12 schools, as required by state and federal law.\n\nThere are four elements included in this dataset:\n<ul><li>Reporting Element 1: The number and percent of ELs who make progress towards English language proficiency</li><li>Reporting Element 2: The number and percent of ELs who attain an ACCESS score indicating English language proficiency</li><li>Reporting Element 3: The number and percentage of ELs who exit English learner classification based on their attainment of English language proficiency</li><li>Reporting Element 5: The number and percentage of ELs who have not attained English proficiency within six years of initial classification as an English learner</li></ul>Reporting Element 4 (the number and percentage of former ELs who have met challenging state academic standards for each of the four years after exiting EL status) is not included in this dataset. For more information about the test administration and reporting elements, please see the <a href=\"https://www.doe.mass.edu/mcas/access/default.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WIDA ACCESS</a> page on the Department of Elementary and Secondary Education's website.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site: \n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/accessreportingelements.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ACCESS for ELLs Reporting Elements</a>",
